      "title": "How to Use \u2014 hypbr Procedural Material",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## hypbr \u2014 Procedural 16-Map Material + Live 3D & Video\n\nGenerate **100% MIT-licensed**, mathematically seamless **16-map PBR materials** (no photo needed), inspect live in **Texture Viewer Pro**, render a **3D preview video**, and export glTF/GLB.\n\n### Quick Steps\n1. **Synthesize Seamless Material**:\n   - `material`: Default is `chainlink_fence_galvanized` (over/under diamond wire weave, rust streaks, and transparent `opacity` holes).\n   - `transparency`: `auto` writes `opacity.png` only for cutout materials (>0.5% holes). Set `off` to force opaque.\n2. **Texture Viewer Pro (Live 3D)**: `alpha_map` is wired for `chainlink_fence_galvanized` cutout transparency. If you switch to an opaque material, disconnect `alpha_map` for crisp opaque sorting. Load `ComfyUI-hypbr/assets/cylinder.glb` or `rounded_cube.glb` via its GLB button!\n3. **Render 3D Video**: Uses `lightorbit` by default so orbiting sunlight casts **real diamond mesh shadows** onto the background wall & floor.\n4. **Export**: Writes `glb` with `alphaMode: \"MASK\"` and `doubleSided: true` when cutout is active (strictly `OPAQUE` otherwise)."
      ]
    },
